{
  "id": "remint-word-status",
  "title": "Re-mint: a word status set in the window is discarded, also for a word created in the window",
  "covers": [
    "re-mint selection (SYNC.md 10.4 step 1): word.status_set / word.status_cleared have no reference, so they meet a clock code themselves and are discarded",
    "word_status is keyed by entry_seq, shared by every replica (dictionary browsing, other devices, jpdb import): an estimated time must not decide it"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "A's clock jumps 10 days ahead; offline, A adds word 3000001 (note + card) and, a minute later, marks it never_forget.",
    "Meanwhile (in real time, a day later) B marks the same entry ignored from the dictionary (seq 1).",
    "A pushes with the clock still wrong: note.created and word.status_set are clock_ahead, card.created is unknown_reference.",
    "Re-mint re-mints the note and the card. The status set is discarded: re-minted at the estimated time it would lose to B's later choice anyway, but in general it would decide a register other replicas write on an estimate. B's status stands; the user sets the status again if wanted.",
    "A also reviewed the new card an hour after creating it (unknown_reference). It is re-minted in step 6b with a new id and reviewed_at shifted by the same delta as the creations, so it stays an hour after its card. `remint` lists the inputs; tools/validate.py recomputes the selection and the shift."
  ],
